You're not serious, are you? Sure, death rays can be a nuisance, but
reflection isn't THAT hard to get. Here's a statistic: 50% of games
contain an "oR in Sokoban. On the average, 50% of games have a shield
of reflection in Perseus' statue (25% chance in half, 75% in the other
half). So 75% of games (at least in vanilla; I'm not sure about
SLASH'EM) are _guaranteed_ to contain a source of reflection. And the
odds of meeting a /oD-wielding creature before Medusa, despite your
experience, are not that large (except maybe in Ludios, so stay out of
Ludios if you don't have reflection or MR). Those cases where you meet
a dwarf/goblin/whatever with a /oD just stand out in your mind among
all the others where you were killed by your own stupidity (I don't
mean to call you stupid; heck, most of MY deaths are attributable to
stupidity, particularly the really good characters). Getting good at
NetHack requires you to improve your playing skills to the point that
cases like yours don't really matter, because you can just fire up
another char and easily make him/her as good as the last one, so it's
no great loss.

Disclaimer: The above description definitely does not apply to me. I
have never ascended, and am hardly a NetHack god. My very best
character ever was lost to a death ray, but only because she committed
the aforementioned Ludios blunder. Other causes of death for top
characters are similarly stupid, like going down a staircase burdened
wielding a cockatrice corpse and trying to take on the priestess of
Mitra in her own temple (the priestess got credit for the kill, but
Mitra gave her a LOT of help).

